From: Taehyun Kim <dice.thkim@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:53:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] cpuinfo: Mark the DOS build's CPUID check with
 DOS_CPUIDChecked

A symbol the ScummVM DOS port looks for (and links against), so that an
SDL3 built without the in-out has_CPUID - which runs CPUID on a 486 -
is refused at build time instead of failing on the 486 itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01429qJytiMpcCADjppM2jV4
---
 src/cpuinfo/SDL_cpuinfo.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cpuinfo/SDL_cpuinfo.c b/src/cpuinfo/SDL_cpuinfo.c
index eaa323111..d3fa0eeaa 100644
--- a/src/cpuinfo/SDL_cpuinfo.c
+++ b/src/cpuinfo/SDL_cpuinfo.c
@@ -134,6 +134,13 @@ static void illegal_instruction(int sig)
 }
 #endif // HAVE_SETJMP
 
+#ifdef SDL_PLATFORM_DOS
+/* Marks a build with the in-out has_CPUID below, which a 486 needs: the
+   ScummVM DOS port refuses (and fails to link against) an SDL3 without it. */
+extern const int DOS_CPUIDChecked;
+const int DOS_CPUIDChecked = 1;
+#endif
+
 static int CPU_haveCPUID(void)
 {
     /* The asm below only stores 1 when CPUID exists: has_CPUID is an in-out
